---
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components'
import DiagramLabel from './DiagramLabel.astro'
import Tag from './Tag.astro'

// The two readings of one agent, drawn for a Staff SDET or a CTO deciding whether the suite can be
// trusted. Same agent, same pinned ports, same traces; what differs is the QUESTION, and therefore
// what you do with variance. Read one way it is the regression lane: deterministic, byte stable,
// gates the merge, a red is a real regression. Read the other it is the measurement lane: a rate
// with an interval, gated on the interval's lower bound. Conflate them and both lie. The structure
// of the harness lives in HarnessMap; this figure is only the two readings. Static, no state.
//
// The counts are real. `uv run --frozen pytest` -> "573 passed in 2.44s" (573 tests across 15 files).
// Re-run it and the count is identical, which is the claim being made.
//
// Two honesty notes the earlier draft got wrong. First, the count was 200; it is 573. Second, the
// measurement lane is NOT a nightly live sweep. `task measure` replays committed cassettes and is
// hermetic today, so it opens no socket either. The two lanes differ by question, not by egress.
// The risk labels below are the shapes the measurement lane reports on, drawn from the probes and
// graders in the tree (probes/metamorphic.py, probes/poison.py, probes/mutation.py, evals/gate.py).

const risks = ['retrieval hit rate', 'metamorphic invariants', 'mutation kill rate', 'poison resistance']
---

<div class="not-prose my-10 border border-border-dark bg-surface rounded-lg overflow-hidden" data-harness>
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-3 bg-surface-container-high border-b border-border-dark flex-wrap">
    <DiagramLabel icon="material-symbols:vertical-split-outline" label="Two machines · one agent, two readings" />
    <span class="hs-note">same agent · same pinned ports · same traces; what differs is the question</span>
  </div>

  <div class="p-5 flex flex-col gap-0">
    <div class="hs-lanes">
      {/* regression lane */}
      <div class="hs-lane">
        <div class="hs-lane-head">
          <span class="hs-box-h"><Icon name="material-symbols:check-circle-outline" class="text-[15px]" />Regression lane</span>
          <Tag label="task test" variant="neutral" />
        </div>
        <p class="hs-q">“did a pinned behaviour change?”</p>
        <ul class="hs-list">
          <li>model <b>replayed</b> from cassette · zero egress</li>
          <li>binary · gates the merge</li>
          <li>flickers never: a red is a real regression</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="hs-runs">
          <span class="hs-run"><Icon name="material-symbols:terminal" class="text-[12px]" />task test<b>573 passed</b></span>
          <span class="hs-run"><Icon name="material-symbols:replay" class="text-[12px]" />re-run<b>573 passed</b></span>
          <span class="hs-bytes"><Icon name="material-symbols:check" class="text-[12px]" />identical count · no keys, no network</span>
        </div>
        <span class="hs-out"><Icon name="material-symbols:block" class="text-[13px]" />must eliminate variance</span>
      </div>

      {/* eval lane */}
      <div class="hs-lane hs-lane-accent">
        <div class="hs-lane-head">
          <span class="hs-box-h"><Icon name="material-symbols:insights" class="text-[15px]" />Measurement lane</span>
          <Tag label="task measure" variant="solid" />
        </div>
        <p class="hs-q">“how good is it, and do we know that well enough to act?”</p>
        <ul class="hs-list">
          <li>the agent driven through its ports by a <b>separate</b> grader</li>
          <li>reports a <b>rate with an interval</b>, never a bare point</li>
          <li>gates on the interval's <b>lower bound</b>, not the point</li>
          <li>three verdicts: PASS, FAIL, and <b>QUARANTINE</b> when the interval is too wide to call</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="hs-risks" aria-label="Business-risk outcomes">
          {risks.map((r) => <span class="hs-risk">{r}</span>)}
        </div>
        <span class="hs-out"><Icon name="material-symbols:check" class="text-[13px]" />must embrace variance</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="hs-legend">
      Two machines, on purpose. The regression suite kills variance so a red means a regression; the
      measurement lane quantifies variance because that is the question it was asked. Re-run the merge lane
      and the count is identical: a flake there is broken determinism, not a moody model. Build one machine
      to answer both and it lies about both. Both lanes replay committed cassettes today, so the difference
      between them is not the network, it is what a number is allowed to be used for.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<style is:global>
  [data-harness] .hs-note { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  [data-harness] .hs-box-h {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem;
    color: var(--color-text-primary); font-weight: 500; font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  [data-harness] .hs-lanes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.85rem; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { [data-harness] .hs-lanes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  [data-harness] .hs-lane {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-dark); background: var(--color-surface-container-low);
    border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
  }
  [data-harness] .hs-lane-accent {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 50%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 6%, transparent);
  }
  [data-harness] .hs-lane-head { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.5rem; }
  [data-harness] .hs-q { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--color-text-primary); }
  [data-harness] .hs-list { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; }
  [data-harness] .hs-list li {
    position: relative; padding-left: 0.95rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.5;
  }
  [data-harness] .hs-list li::before { content: '-'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  [data-harness] .hs-list b { color: var(--color-text-primary); font-weight: 500; }

  /* byte-stable proof (replaces the old terminal block) */
  [data-harness] .hs-runs { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; margin-top: 0.1rem; }
  [data-harness] .hs-run {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.3rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.64rem; color: var(--color-text-muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-dark); background: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 0.15rem 0.45rem;
  }
  [data-harness] .hs-run b { color: var(--color-primary); font-weight: 500; }
  [data-harness] .hs-bytes {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.25rem; flex-basis: 100%;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.6rem; color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  [data-harness] .hs-risks { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.3rem; margin-top: 0.1rem; }
  [data-harness] .hs-risk {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.62rem; color: var(--color-primary);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 35%, transparent);
    border-radius: 999px; padding: 0.1rem 0.45rem;
  }
  [data-harness] .hs-out {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.3rem; margin-top: 0.2rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.64rem; color: var(--color-text-muted);
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--color-border-dark); padding-top: 0.4rem;
  }
  [data-harness] .hs-legend {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  [data-harness] .hs-legend b { color: var(--color-text-primary); font-weight: 500; }
</style>
